qsh for Debian
==============

This directory is upstream's starting point for the Debian package; it lives in the upstream
repository as packaging/debian/ and is copied to debian/ to build:

    cp -r packaging/debian debian
    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc                       # dependencies from librust-*-dev
    DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=pkg.qsh.vendored \
      dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc                     # dependencies from vendor/ (cargo vendor)

Binary packages: qsh-client (qsh) and qsh-server (qsh-server and its systemd user unit), split
like openssh-client / openssh-server and mosh, so servers need not carry the client.

Generated files: man/*.1, man/*.5 and completions/* are generated from the command-line
definitions upstream and committed to the repository; the release tarball contains them.

Dependencies: every crate qsh uses (tokio, quinn, rustls with ring, rcgen, clap, serde,
serde_json, libc) is packaged in Debian; the version bounds in debian/control follow the
workspace Cargo.toml. With the pkg.qsh.vendored profile the vendored crates are built instead
and debian/copyright must be extended to cover them (see the vendor/* stanza).

The cargo feature self-install (`qsh install HOST`, which downloads release binaries) is not
enabled: the Debian build performs no network access at build time or at runtime.

 -- yzfly <zphyix@gmail.com>, placeholder date
